    "isNew": false,
    "summary": {
      "en": "The World Bank is building an AI tool to extract causal evidence from development research, guiding $220B in annual aid allocation.",
      "zh": "世界銀行正在開發 AI 工具從發展研究文獻中提取因果證據，為每年 2,200 億美元的援助資金分配提供依據。"
    },
    "overview": {
      "en": "The World Bank is developing ImpactAI, a tool that leverages large language models to extract key causal impact data from thousands of development intervention studies. The system automates extraction of economic relationships between interventions and outcomes from randomized controlled trials, standardizing findings into comparable metrics. The ultimate goal is to empower decision-makers to allocate $220 billion in annual aid and trillions in annual impact investing more effectively. ImpactAI launched publicly in October 2025.",
      "zh": "世界銀行正在開發 ImpactAI，一個利用大型語言模型從數千項發展干預研究中提取關鍵因果影響資料的工具。系統自動從隨機對照試驗中提取干預與結果之間的經濟關係，將研究結果標準化為可比較的指標。最終目標是幫助決策者更有效地分配每年 2,200 億美元的援助資金和數兆美元的影響力投資。ImpactAI 於 2025 年 10 月公開發布。"
    },
    "highlights": {
      "en": [
        "ImpactAI extracts causal evidence from thousands of development intervention studies.",
        "Aims to improve allocation of $220 billion in annual aid and trillions in impact investing.",
        "Automates data extraction from randomized controlled trials and standardizes findings.",
        "Publicly launched October 2025 as a conversational AI agent for policymakers."
      ],
      "zh": [
        "ImpactAI 從數千項發展干預研究中提取因果證據。",
        "旨在改善每年 2,200 億美元援助資金和數兆美元影響力投資的分配。",
        "自動從隨機對照試驗中提取資料並標準化研究結果。",
        "2025 年 10 月作為面向政策制定者的對話式 AI 代理程式公開發布。"
      ]
    },
